1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,060
The Rimac Nevera weighs more than two

2
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:05,625
tonnes, as much as a big family

3
00:00:05,625 --> 00:00:05,955
SUV.

4
00:00:06,135 --> 00:00:08,613
It has no engine sound,

5
00:00:08,613 --> 00:00:11,952
no gear changes and no exhaust.

6
00:00:12,132 --> 00:00:15,121
And it can reach one hundred kilometres

7
00:00:15,121 --> 00:00:17,421
per hour in under two seconds,

8
00:00:17,421 --> 00:00:20,716
faster than almost any petrol supercar ever

9
00:00:20,716 --> 00:00:21,176
built.

10
00:00:21,356 --> 00:00:21,577
How?

11
00:00:21,757 --> 00:00:25,533
Today, ten parts of an electric hypercar,

12
00:00:25,533 --> 00:00:28,111
and why each one makes it so

13
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:28,572
fast.

14
00:00:28,921 --> 00:00:30,110
For a century,

15
00:00:30,110 --> 00:00:33,590
the fastest cars were built around bigger

16
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:35,202
and louder engines.

17
00:00:35,382 --> 00:00:38,227
Then electric motors changed the rules.

18
00:00:38,407 --> 00:00:41,261
They work in a completely different way

19
00:00:41,261 --> 00:00:42,797
from a petrol engine,

20
00:00:42,797 --> 00:00:45,797
and almost every advantage of an electric

21
00:00:45,797 --> 00:00:48,431
hypercar comes from that difference,

22
00:00:48,431 --> 00:00:50,992
and from the battery that feeds it.

23
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:54,168
As always, every fact here comes from

24
00:00:54,168 --> 00:00:55,313
a named source,

25
00:00:55,313 --> 00:00:58,444
the car makers and automotive references,

26
00:00:58,444 --> 00:01:00,735
all listed in the description.

27
00:01:00,915 --> 00:01:02,355
Let's start with the motor.

28
00:01:02,704 --> 00:01:05,232
Why does an electric motor pull so

29
00:01:05,232 --> 00:01:06,942
hard from a standstill?

30
00:01:07,122 --> 00:01:10,189
A petrol engine makes its best force

31
00:01:10,189 --> 00:01:12,660
only at higher engine speeds.

32
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,640
It has to rev up first.

33
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:17,975
An electric motor makes its full pulling

34
00:01:17,975 --> 00:01:19,631
force, called torque,

35
00:01:19,631 --> 00:01:22,471
from the very first moment it turns.

36
00:01:22,651 --> 00:01:24,225
There is no waiting,

37
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:25,170
no build up.

38
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:26,465
Press the pedal,

39
00:01:26,465 --> 00:01:28,554
and all of it arrives at once.

40
00:01:28,904 --> 00:01:31,869
This is why even ordinary electric cars

41
00:01:31,869 --> 00:01:34,605
feel quick away from traffic lights.

42
00:01:34,785 --> 00:01:36,041
In a petrol car,

43
00:01:36,041 --> 00:01:39,025
the engine, the clutch and the gearbox

44
00:01:39,025 --> 00:01:40,752
have to work together,

45
00:01:40,752 --> 00:01:44,050
and every gear change interrupts the push.

46
00:01:44,230 --> 00:01:45,822
In an electric car,

47
00:01:45,822 --> 00:01:48,586
the force is smooth and constant,

48
00:01:48,586 --> 00:01:50,429
all the way from zero.

49
00:01:50,779 --> 00:01:54,030
The motor itself is surprisingly simple.

50
00:01:54,210 --> 00:01:56,910
Magnets and coils of copper wire,

51
00:01:56,910 --> 00:01:59,528
with one moving part that spins.

52
00:01:59,708 --> 00:02:02,049
No pistons, no valves,

53
00:02:02,049 --> 00:02:03,539
no explosions.

54
00:02:03,719 --> 00:02:05,729
A motor the size of a large

55
00:02:05,729 --> 00:02:09,152
watermelon can produce hundreds of horsepower.

56
00:02:09,332 --> 00:02:12,349
Simple, compact and brutally strong,

57
00:02:12,349 --> 00:02:15,115
it is the heart of every electric

58
00:02:15,115 --> 00:02:15,869
hypercar.

59
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:18,872
Why does the Rimac Nevera have four

60
00:02:18,872 --> 00:02:20,085
electric motors?

61
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:21,751
One for each wheel.

62
00:02:21,931 --> 00:02:25,005
Together, they produce close to two thousand

63
00:02:25,005 --> 00:02:25,774
horsepower.

64
00:02:25,954 --> 00:02:28,427
But the real reason is control.

65
00:02:28,607 --> 00:02:31,230
Each wheel can be given exactly the

66
00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:34,078
right amount of force at every moment,

67
00:02:34,078 --> 00:02:36,176
independently of the others.

68
00:02:36,526 --> 00:02:38,872
This is called torque vectoring.

69
00:02:39,052 --> 00:02:39,983
In a corner,

70
00:02:39,983 --> 00:02:42,699
the car can push the outside wheels

71
00:02:42,699 --> 00:02:45,027
harder than the inside wheels,

72
00:02:45,027 --> 00:02:46,656
helping the car turn.

73
00:02:46,836 --> 00:02:48,307
On a slippery surface,

74
00:02:48,307 --> 00:02:50,178
it can reduce the force on a

75
00:02:50,178 --> 00:02:52,049
wheel that is about to spin.

76
00:02:52,229 --> 00:02:55,978
A petrol car needs complex differentials to

77
00:02:55,978 --> 00:02:57,372
do some of this.

78
00:02:57,552 --> 00:03:00,083
Four motors do it directly.

79
00:03:00,433 --> 00:03:03,630
Electric motors can change their force far

80
00:03:03,630 --> 00:03:05,913
faster than any petrol engine.

81
00:03:06,093 --> 00:03:09,424
The car's computer adjusts each wheel many

82
00:03:09,424 --> 00:03:10,772
times per second.

83
00:03:10,952 --> 00:03:13,669
At launch, that means the tyres stay

84
00:03:13,669 --> 00:03:15,556
at the very edge of grip,

85
00:03:15,556 --> 00:03:16,838
without spinning.

86
00:03:17,018 --> 00:03:19,338
The four motors are not just about

87
00:03:19,338 --> 00:03:19,747
power.

88
00:03:19,927 --> 00:03:21,693
They are about using every bit of

89
00:03:21,693 --> 00:03:21,854
it.

90
00:03:22,204 --> 00:03:24,695
Why is the battery of an electric

91
00:03:24,695 --> 00:03:26,581
hypercar under the floor?

92
00:03:26,761 --> 00:03:28,868
Because it is the heaviest part of

93
00:03:28,868 --> 00:03:30,975
the car, and the lower the weight,

94
00:03:30,975 --> 00:03:32,648
the better the car handles.

95
00:03:32,828 --> 00:03:35,948
Putting hundreds of kilograms of battery at

96
00:03:35,948 --> 00:03:38,270
the very bottom of the car gives

97
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:40,592
it a very low centre of gravity,

98
00:03:40,592 --> 00:03:42,986
lower than most petrol supercars.

99
00:03:43,337 --> 00:03:46,092
A low centre of gravity means the

100
00:03:46,092 --> 00:03:49,014
car leans less in corners and stays

101
00:03:49,014 --> 00:03:52,520
more stable when braking and accelerating.

102
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:53,697
In the Nevera,

103
00:03:53,697 --> 00:03:55,976
the battery is shaped like an H,

104
00:03:55,976 --> 00:03:58,397
and runs through the middle of the

105
00:03:58,397 --> 00:04:00,676
car, behind and under the seats.

106
00:04:00,856 --> 00:04:03,192
It is also part of the structure,

107
00:04:03,192 --> 00:04:05,245
making the whole car stiffer.

108
00:04:05,595 --> 00:04:07,666
That is how a car that weighs

109
00:04:07,666 --> 00:04:10,309
over two tonnes can still corner like

110
00:04:10,309 --> 00:04:11,667
a much lighter car.

111
00:04:11,847 --> 00:04:13,314
The weight is there,

112
00:04:13,314 --> 00:04:15,516
but it is in the best possible

113
00:04:15,516 --> 00:04:15,956
place.

114
00:04:16,136 --> 00:04:17,472
In a petrol car,

115
00:04:17,472 --> 00:04:19,225
the engine sits high.

116
00:04:19,405 --> 00:04:20,983
In an electric car,

117
00:04:20,983 --> 00:04:23,309
the heaviest part lies flat,

118
00:04:23,309 --> 00:04:25,802
right where engineers want it.

119
00:04:26,152 --> 00:04:29,162
Why do most electric cars have only

120
00:04:29,162 --> 00:04:29,936
one gear?

121
00:04:30,116 --> 00:04:33,416
Because an electric motor can spin very

122
00:04:33,416 --> 00:04:36,715
fast and still make strong force across

123
00:04:36,715 --> 00:04:38,661
a huge range of speeds.

124
00:04:38,841 --> 00:04:41,652
A petrol engine works well only in

125
00:04:41,652 --> 00:04:42,810
a narrow band,

126
00:04:42,810 --> 00:04:45,290
so it needs many gears to stay

127
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:46,365
in that band.

128
00:04:46,545 --> 00:04:48,588
An electric motor does not.

129
00:04:48,938 --> 00:04:52,207
A single gear means no gear changes,

130
00:04:52,207 --> 00:04:55,114
and no interruption in the push.

131
00:04:55,294 --> 00:04:57,998
The acceleration is one smooth,

132
00:04:57,998 --> 00:05:01,226
unbroken surge from zero to very high

133
00:05:01,226 --> 00:05:01,749
speed.

134
00:05:01,929 --> 00:05:04,396
It also means fewer moving parts,

135
00:05:04,396 --> 00:05:06,863
less weight and less to go wrong.

136
00:05:07,043 --> 00:05:10,333
For acceleration, one gear is often the

137
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:11,177
best gear.

138
00:05:11,526 --> 00:05:13,094
There are exceptions.

139
00:05:13,274 --> 00:05:15,886
The Porsche Taycan has a two speed

140
00:05:15,886 --> 00:05:17,883
gearbox on its rear motor.

141
00:05:18,063 --> 00:05:21,022
The first gear gives a stronger launch,

142
00:05:21,022 --> 00:05:23,601
and the second lets the motor spin

143
00:05:23,601 --> 00:05:25,194
slower at high speed,

144
00:05:25,194 --> 00:05:28,001
which helps efficiency and top speed.

145
00:05:28,181 --> 00:05:31,397
Engineers still debate which approach is better.

146
00:05:31,577 --> 00:05:33,812
But for most electric cars,

147
00:05:33,812 --> 00:05:35,385
one gear is enough.

148
00:05:35,735 --> 00:05:38,251
Why is a small metal box called

149
00:05:38,251 --> 00:05:41,335
the inverter one of the most important

150
00:05:41,335 --> 00:05:43,363
parts of an electric car?

151
00:05:43,543 --> 00:05:47,187
The battery stores electricity as direct current,

152
00:05:47,187 --> 00:05:49,046
flowing in one direction.

153
00:05:49,226 --> 00:05:53,272
Most electric car motors need alternating current,

154
00:05:53,272 --> 00:05:56,993
which changes direction many times per second.

155
00:05:57,173 --> 00:05:59,658
The inverter converts one into the other.

156
00:06:00,007 --> 00:06:02,443
By changing how fast and how strongly

157
00:06:02,443 --> 00:06:03,957
the current alternates,

158
00:06:03,957 --> 00:06:06,524
the inverter controls the speed and the

159
00:06:06,524 --> 00:06:07,775
force of the motor.

160
00:06:07,955 --> 00:06:09,899
It is the part that turns your

161
00:06:09,899 --> 00:06:11,844
foot on the pedal into motion.

162
00:06:12,024 --> 00:06:13,094
In a hypercar,

163
00:06:13,094 --> 00:06:15,311
it handles enormous currents,

164
00:06:15,311 --> 00:06:16,840
hundreds of amperes,

165
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:19,745
switching them on and off thousands of

166
00:06:19,745 --> 00:06:21,045
times per second.

167
00:06:21,394 --> 00:06:25,309
Modern inverters use a material called silicon

168
00:06:25,309 --> 00:06:28,799
carbide, which wastes less energy as heat

169
00:06:28,799 --> 00:06:31,437
and can handle higher voltages.

170
00:06:31,617 --> 00:06:33,957
Tesla was one of the first to

171
00:06:33,957 --> 00:06:36,540
use it in a mass production car.

172
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:39,875
Less wasted heat means more power reaches

173
00:06:39,875 --> 00:06:42,569
the wheels, and more range from the

174
00:06:42,569 --> 00:06:43,570
same battery.

175
00:06:43,919 --> 00:06:46,666
Why can a hypercar battery deliver so

176
00:06:46,666 --> 00:06:48,076
much power at once?

177
00:06:48,256 --> 00:06:50,938
Because it is designed for power,

178
00:06:50,938 --> 00:06:52,157
not just range.

179
00:06:52,337 --> 00:06:55,284
A battery is made of thousands of

180
00:06:55,284 --> 00:06:55,820
cells.

181
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,547
Some cells are built to store as

182
00:06:58,547 --> 00:07:00,458
much energy as possible.

183
00:07:00,638 --> 00:07:04,055
Others are built to release energy very

184
00:07:04,055 --> 00:07:04,493
fast.

185
00:07:04,673 --> 00:07:07,960
Hypercars use cells that can do both,

186
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:09,293
at a high cost.

187
00:07:09,643 --> 00:07:12,591
Releasing more than a megawatt from a

188
00:07:12,591 --> 00:07:14,821
battery is a huge challenge.

189
00:07:15,001 --> 00:07:16,774
The cells heat up quickly,

190
00:07:16,774 --> 00:07:19,843
and every connection between them must handle

191
00:07:19,843 --> 00:07:20,934
a large current.

192
00:07:21,114 --> 00:07:24,445
The Nevera's battery is designed to deliver

193
00:07:24,445 --> 00:07:27,776
the power of about two thousand horsepower,

194
00:07:27,776 --> 00:07:30,565
enough to supply many homes at once.

195
00:07:30,914 --> 00:07:33,541
This is the real secret of electric

196
00:07:33,541 --> 00:07:33,991
speed.

197
00:07:34,171 --> 00:07:37,074
A powerful motor is easy to build.

198
00:07:37,254 --> 00:07:39,815
Feeding it with enough electricity,

199
00:07:39,815 --> 00:07:40,986
for long enough,

200
00:07:40,986 --> 00:07:43,767
without overheating, is the hard part.

201
00:07:43,947 --> 00:07:46,017
The battery is not just a fuel

202
00:07:46,017 --> 00:07:46,362
tank.

203
00:07:46,542 --> 00:07:48,639
It is the part that decides how

204
00:07:48,639 --> 00:07:50,466
fast the car can really go.

205
00:07:50,815 --> 00:07:53,427
Why does an electric hypercar need so

206
00:07:53,427 --> 00:07:54,345
much cooling?

207
00:07:54,525 --> 00:07:57,611
Because batteries and motors do not like

208
00:07:57,611 --> 00:07:57,996
heat.

209
00:07:58,176 --> 00:08:01,217
When a battery delivers a huge amount

210
00:08:01,217 --> 00:08:03,436
of power, it warms up fast.

211
00:08:03,616 --> 00:08:06,642
Too hot, and the cells age quickly

212
00:08:06,642 --> 00:08:09,223
or can even become dangerous.

213
00:08:09,403 --> 00:08:11,972
So the car limits its power before

214
00:08:11,972 --> 00:08:13,861
the battery gets too hot.

215
00:08:14,211 --> 00:08:16,904
That is why hypercars have liquid cooling

216
00:08:16,904 --> 00:08:19,136
running between the battery cells,

217
00:08:19,136 --> 00:08:22,026
around the motors and through the inverters,

218
00:08:22,026 --> 00:08:24,258
with radiators in the front of the

219
00:08:24,258 --> 00:08:24,521
car.

220
00:08:24,701 --> 00:08:25,937
On a race track,

221
00:08:25,937 --> 00:08:28,872
the cooling decides how many fast laps

222
00:08:28,872 --> 00:08:31,035
the car can do before it has

223
00:08:31,035 --> 00:08:32,271
to reduce power.

224
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:35,564
A petrol supercar can run at full

225
00:08:35,564 --> 00:08:38,240
speed until the tank is empty.

226
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:41,675
Many electric cars can deliver full power

227
00:08:41,675 --> 00:08:42,945
in short bursts,

228
00:08:42,945 --> 00:08:44,294
but not for long.

229
00:08:44,474 --> 00:08:47,898
Better cooling is what separates an electric

230
00:08:47,898 --> 00:08:50,933
hypercar that only wins drag races from

231
00:08:50,933 --> 00:08:53,579
one that can survive a whole track

232
00:08:53,579 --> 00:08:53,890
day.

233
00:08:54,239 --> 00:08:56,953
Why are some new electric motors flat,

234
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:58,024
like a pancake?

235
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:00,898
They are called axial flux motors.

236
00:09:01,078 --> 00:09:02,564
In a normal motor,

237
00:09:02,564 --> 00:09:06,031
the magnetic field crosses the gap between

238
00:09:06,031 --> 00:09:09,085
a spinning cylinder and a ring around

239
00:09:09,085 --> 00:09:09,333
it.

240
00:09:09,513 --> 00:09:11,512
In an axial flux motor,

241
00:09:11,512 --> 00:09:14,121
the field runs along the axis,

242
00:09:14,121 --> 00:09:17,512
between flat discs placed side by side.

243
00:09:17,861 --> 00:09:20,801
That layout puts the magnets further from

244
00:09:20,801 --> 00:09:23,813
the centre, where they have more leverage,

245
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:26,323
so the motor can produce more force

246
00:09:26,323 --> 00:09:28,043
for its size and weight.

247
00:09:28,223 --> 00:09:31,250
A flat motor can also fit between

248
00:09:31,250 --> 00:09:33,451
an engine and a gearbox,

249
00:09:33,451 --> 00:09:36,385
where a long cylinder would not.

250
00:09:36,565 --> 00:09:40,745
Ferrari uses one in its hybrid SF90.

251
00:09:41,094 --> 00:09:44,442
Axial flux motors are harder to build

252
00:09:44,442 --> 00:09:47,700
and cool, which is why they appeared

253
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:49,872
first in expensive cars.

254
00:09:50,052 --> 00:09:51,867
But as production grows,

255
00:09:51,867 --> 00:09:55,044
they may spread to everyday electric cars.

256
00:09:55,224 --> 00:09:58,594
In engineering, the most exotic parts of

257
00:09:58,594 --> 00:10:02,554
today's hypercars often become the normal parts

258
00:10:02,554 --> 00:10:04,744
of tomorrow's family cars.

259
00:10:05,094 --> 00:10:07,443
Why are the tyres the real limit

260
00:10:07,443 --> 00:10:09,204
of an electric hypercar?

261
00:10:09,384 --> 00:10:12,082
Because the motors can deliver more force

262
00:10:12,082 --> 00:10:13,990
than the tyres can put on the

263
00:10:13,990 --> 00:10:14,319
road.

264
00:10:14,499 --> 00:10:16,179
At a standing start,

265
00:10:16,179 --> 00:10:19,959
two thousand horsepower would simply spin the

266
00:10:19,959 --> 00:10:20,547
wheels.

267
00:10:20,727 --> 00:10:22,781
The car is only as fast as

268
00:10:22,781 --> 00:10:25,387
the grip of four small patches of

269
00:10:25,387 --> 00:10:27,914
rubber, each about the size of a

270
00:10:27,914 --> 00:10:28,309
hand.

271
00:10:28,658 --> 00:10:31,779
That is why hypercars use special soft

272
00:10:31,779 --> 00:10:35,474
tyres, sometimes developed just for that car.

273
00:10:35,654 --> 00:10:37,818
Soft rubber grips better,

274
00:10:37,818 --> 00:10:39,636
but wears out faster.

275
00:10:39,816 --> 00:10:41,162
On a cold road,

276
00:10:41,162 --> 00:10:43,856
even the best tyres grip less.

277
00:10:44,036 --> 00:10:47,162
The record runs of electric hypercars are

278
00:10:47,162 --> 00:10:48,458
done on prepared,

279
00:10:48,458 --> 00:10:51,050
warm surfaces, to get every bit of

280
00:10:51,050 --> 00:10:51,432
grip.

281
00:10:51,781 --> 00:10:54,533
It is a funny problem for engineers.

282
00:10:54,713 --> 00:10:55,741
For a century,

283
00:10:55,741 --> 00:10:58,533
the challenge was making enough power.

284
00:10:58,713 --> 00:11:01,569
Now the challenge is putting it down.

285
00:11:01,749 --> 00:11:04,412
An electric hypercar has more power than

286
00:11:04,412 --> 00:11:06,477
its tyres can use at low speed,

287
00:11:06,477 --> 00:11:08,674
and the computer holds it back to

288
00:11:08,674 --> 00:11:11,072
